Dear Tomás,

Thank you for the report and for the guided tour, which saved me a good deal of time. Two questions arose when I compared the figures against the July report, and I would be grateful for your help with both before I pass the document on to Walter's office.

1. Events ingested rose from 34.9M to 41.2M, an increase of roughly eighteen per cent in a month in which production volume was, to my knowledge, broadly flat. Is that increase attributable entirely to the new packaging-cell sensors, or could a part of it be a double count following the connector update on the twelfth?

2. The report shows fourteen named seats, whereas our order form licenses twelve. Are the two additional seats the Tessera support logins that Yuki mentioned during onboarding, and if so, are they billable?

I should say that neither question is an objection; I simply need to be able to answer them if Walter asks, which he will.

Kind regards,

Simon Achterberg
Procurement Lead | Veritas Components

